ational Petroleum Corp.)"}]]}],["$","div","Project",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-xs text-arbiter-muted font-medium mb-1","children":"Project"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-arbiter-dark","children":"Blackrod SAGD Phase 1"}]]}],["$","div","Sector",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-xs text-arbiter-muted font-medium mb-1","children":"Sector"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-arbiter-dark","children":"Oil Sands, Alberta"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-7 text-arbiter-muted text-base leading-relaxed","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-arbiter-dark mb-3","children":"The Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"At the IPC Blackrod SAGD facility in northern Alberta, the commissioning team faced a challenge common to large capital projects: ensuring that hundreds of vendor-supplied instruments and safety devices were installed, verified, and documented correctly before first startup. With paper-based check sheets, discrepancies could go undetected until they became costly and potentially dangerous problems."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-2xl overflow-hidden aspect-[16/8]","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504307651254-35680f356dfd?w=1000&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80","alt":"Field commissioning work","className":"w-full h-full object-cover"}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-arbiter-dark mb-3","children":"How Arbiter Was Applied"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The team deployed Arbiter's SoftChecks across all flame detector verification workflows. Each instrument was tied to a digital check sheet that required photographic evidence, technician sign-off, and model-number verification against the approved instrument list."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4","children":"During a routine SoftCheck on a bank of flame detectors in the production facility, a technician flagged a model number that did not match the specification. The discrepancy was instantly logged as an Action, assigned to the responsible vendor, and escalated to the commissioning lead — all within the Arbiter platform."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-[#0d2b06] rounded-2xl px-8 py-8 relative overflow-hidden","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.06]","style":{"backgroundImage":"radial-gradient(circle at 1px 1px, #5aaf30 1px, transparent 0)","backgroundSize":"24px 24px"}}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[#6dc744] text-5xl font-serif leading-none mb-3 opacity-60","children":"\""}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-white text-lg font-medium italic leading-snug","children":"Without Arbiter, that discrepancy might not have surfaced until after first fire. The digital trail gave us the proof we needed to hold the vendor accountable on the spot."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-white/45 text-sm mt-4 font-medium","children":"Commissioning Lead, IPC Blackrod"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-arbiter-dark mb-3","children":"The Outcome"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The vendor was required to replace the incorrect units before the startup sequence could proceed. Because Arbiter captured the full timeline — detection, assignment, rectification, and re-verification — the project team had a complete, timestamped audit trail ready for the regulatory review."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4","children":"At project handover, the Dossier feature auto-compiled every check sheet, action, and attached document into a single digital turnover package, delivered to the client in hours rather than weeks."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-arbiter-gray-bg border border-arbiter-border rounded-2xl p-7","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold text-arbiter-green tracking-[0.2em] u